  "notes": "Sub-objective ids (1.1.a, 1.1.b, ...) are assigned by this site in the order B.1.3 prints the bullets. \"details\" holds every deeper line, flattened as \"Parent > child\". B.1.3's own outline numbers (such as \"4.1 -\" and \"4.1.1 -\") and its Lesson Index column are left out. Wording, capitals, and spacing are as B.1.3 prints them, including the space after the second slash in \"Playbooks/templates/ reusable tasks\"; the only character changed is the stray dash in \"Bayonet Neill-Concelman (BNC)\", typed as a plain hyphen. Lines that B.1.3 prints at the same level as their heading are nested under that heading: in 3.2.a, \"v2c\" and \"v3\" under SNMP \"Versions\"; in 3.4.b, the seven record types (\"Address (A)\" to \"Pointer\") under DNS \"Record types\", and \"Forward\" and \"Reverse\" under DNS \"Zone types\". \"Authoritative vs. non-authoritative\", \"Primary vs. secondary\", and \"Recursive\" stay DNS lines beside \"Record types\" and \"Zone types\": Reading 6.5.7 names forward and reverse lookup as the two types of zones, and Readings 6.5.3, 6.5.8, and 6.5.9 teach the other three as DNS server and query concepts.",
